Review brief:
Prepare a focused review of how PFAS properties, water chemistry, and reactor operation control foam-fractionation performance.

Required components:
[{"requirement":"Evaluate effects of PFAS chain length and functional group, co-surfactants, organic matter, salts, and competing constituents."},{"requirement":"Compare gas flow, bubble size, residence time, recycle, foam collection, and reactor configuration."},{"requirement":"Interpret removal, recovery, enrichment, mass balance, and volume reduction as distinct performance measures."}]

Task boundaries:
{"constraints":[{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if removal, recovery, enrichment, mass-balance closure, and volume reduction are treated as interchangeable."},{"material_violation_rule":"Triggers if an operating effect is generalized across PFAS structures or matrices without preserving the tested conditions."}],"task_boundaries":"Operating and matrix controls on aqueous PFAS foam fractionation; performance measures must retain their distinct definitions."}

Held-out anchor identifiers:
{"all_blocked_dois":["10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.133182"],"all_blocked_titles":["a review of foam fractionation for the removal of per and polyfluoroalkyl substances pfas from aqueous matrices"],"all_blocked_urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.133182"],"anchor_id":"AR-WE-2024","corpus_source":"2024 - We - A review of foam fractionation for the removal of per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) from aqueous matrices.pdf","doi":"10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.133182","title":"A review of foam fractionation for the removal of per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) from aqueous matrices","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jhazmat.2023.133182"}

